# AI quality

Canonical: technical guide §16–§18.

## Product language

- Practice feedback with evidence and uncertainty — never official scores, pass %, or telc affiliation
- Cite transcript moments; do not fabricate quotations
- State engine controls stage order and timers — models may not rewrite the blueprint

## Implementation

- Validate all structured model output with Zod; reject/retry only on safe failures
- Do not hardcode model names in features — use capability-specific server config
- Version prompts, models, and blueprint together; record latency, usage, and cost
- Reports are async jobs (Postgres job table); never rely on an unawaited serverless promise alone
- Client must not send raw system prompts or arbitrary rubric content
- Bound retries; do not retry validation, authorization, or content-policy failures
- Do not store full prompts/transcripts in error logs

## Release gate

Model/prompt changes need the teacher-reviewed eval set — JSON validity alone is not enough.
Keep AI evals separate from ordinary unit snapshots.
